00:52:32,500 --> 00:52:38,500
Fear is a  1996 American psychological thriller film directed by
James Foley and written by Christopher Crowe.

14
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:41,000
It stars Mark Wahlberg, Reese Witherspoon, William
Petersen, Alyssa Milano and Amy Brenneman.

15
01:00:37,500 --> 01:00:43,500
The film revolves around the wealthy Walker family whose seemingly perfect life is threatened when teenage daughter Nicole
begins dating David McCall, an attractive and mysterious young man who turns out to be a violent sociopath.

16
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
Fear was released by Universal Pictures on April 12, 1996.

17
01:08:42,500 --> 01:08:48,500
The film was largely derided by critics upon its release but became a sleeper
hit in the spring of 1996, grossing $20.8 million at the U.S.

18
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:51,000
box office against a $6.5 million budget.

19
01:16:47,500 --> 01:16:53,500
It has since become a cult film, while at the same time launching teen idol status for its two young leads –
Wahlberg and Witherspoon – who were romantically linked at the time of the movie's premiere.

20
01:20:50,000 --> 01:20:56,000
Wahlberg was nominated for the MTV Movie Award for Best
Villain at the 1997 MTV Movie Awards.

21
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:58,500
The film's own producer, Brian Grazer, described it
as "Fatal Attraction for teens".

22
01:28:55,000 --> 01:29:01,000
The film explores themes of psychopath, father, loss of
virginity, teenage girl, psychological thriller.

23
01:32:57,500 --> 01:33:03,500
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
